1
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:19,610
So, how we feeling, Illinois?
伊利诺伊州，大家感觉怎么样？

2
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:24,460
Oh, can we just take a second to take it all in?
我们能不能花一点时间，感受眼前这一刻？

3
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:29,670
Love you back.
我也爱你们。

4
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:37,460
Illinois, I wish that you could see the view that I see from up here tonight.
伊利诺伊，我真希望你们能看到，今晚我从台上看到的景象。

5
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:47,500
I see a room full of familiar faces, friends old and new, loved ones from every stage of my life,
满屋熟悉的面孔，新老朋友，生命中每个阶段的亲人，

6
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:51,500
People that have been by my side since day one.
以及从第一天起就站在我身旁的人。

7
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,340
Look at the people standing beside you.
看看站在你旁边的人。

8
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:02,600
We are making history and this is the team that made it possible.
我们正在创造历史，而这就是让历史成为可能的团队。

9
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:14,800
Now, if you've seen me on the campaign trail, you probably heard me reference an African proverb that I love.
在竞选路上见过我的人，可能听过我引用一句我很喜欢的非洲谚语。

10
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,920
It says, "If you want to go fast, go alone.
它说：“想走得快，就独自走。

11
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:22,960
If you want to go far, go together."
想走得远，就一起走。”

12
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:26,320
Well, Illinois, look how far we've come.
伊利诺伊，看看我们已经走了多远。

13
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:31,290
And we did it together.
而我们是一起做到的。

14
00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:37,330
Together we did what so many told us was impossible.
一起做到许多人曾说不可能的事。

15
00:01:38,350 --> 00:01:43,610
Together we built a movement that reached every corner of this state.
一起建立了一场遍及全州每个角落的运动。

16
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:51,650
Together we showed that we can center a campaign on the people, not the powerful.
一起证明，一场竞选可以以人民、而非权贵为中心。

17
00:01:52,930 --> 00:01:59,670
And together we made it clear that Illinois is not going backwards.
一起明确表示：伊利诺伊不会倒退。

18
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,410
No.
绝不会。

19
00:02:03,410 --> 00:02:05,820
Let me tell you something about this campaign.
让我告诉你们，这场竞选的一些事。

20
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:10,180
It was never supposed to be easy and it wasn't.
它从一开始就不可能轻松，事实也确实如此。

21
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:15,040
There were low lows, and days when we needed to dig deep.
我们有过低谷，有过必须拼尽最后力气的日子。

22
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:18,380
None of us could have walked this path alone.
没有人能够独自走完这条路。

23
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:20,520
But, we linked arms.
但我们挽起了手臂。

24
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:27,860
We leaned on one another, and together, we have not only won this seat, but we have won it decisively.
我们彼此依靠；最终，我们不仅赢得这个席位，而且赢得干脆、赢得明确。

25
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,960
We did that.
我们做到了。

26
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:39,980
So, tonight, I'm really here to celebrate each and every one of you.
所以今晚，我来到这里，是为你们每一个人庆祝。

27
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:47,900
This campaign wasn't mine, it was ours, and this victory belongs to all of us.
这不是我一个人的竞选，而是我们的竞选；这场胜利，属于所有人。

28
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:52,180
I owe a debt of gratitude to so many of you.
我欠你们许多人一份深深的感谢。

29
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:58,600
First and foremost, I want to give honor to God, who makes all things possible.
首先，我要荣耀上帝，是他让一切皆有可能。

30
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:10,290
Thank you, God, for instilling us with a righteous fight, and for walking with us on this path.
感谢上帝，赋予我们正义的斗志，并与我们一路同行。

31
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:33,186
To my campaign manager, [name unclear], And my amazing campaign team, Tyler, Allison, Marguerite, Morgan, Nicole, Alexis, Anna Lee,
感谢我的竞选经理[姓名听不清]，以及出色的竞选团队：泰勒、艾莉森、玛格丽特、摩根、妮科尔、亚历克西斯、安娜莉，

32
00:03:33,186 --> 00:03:39,420
Charles, Daniel, Fiona, Zena, and Reverend Stan.
查尔斯、丹尼尔、菲奥娜、泽娜，以及斯坦牧师。

33
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:43,860
Thank you for bringing your all each and every day.
感谢你们每一天都全力以赴。

34
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:48,580
You are truly the A-team, and I've been so blessed to be on this journey with you.
你们是真正的王牌团队，能与你们同行，是我的福分。

35
00:03:48,580 --> 00:04:01,520
To the team at Magnify Strategies, Caitlin, Paul, Aaron, Emily, and Leah.
感谢 Magnify Strategies 团队：凯特琳、保罗、亚伦、埃米莉和莉娅。

36
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:06,440
And to Katie Langenfeld and Associates.
感谢凯蒂·兰根费尔德及其团队。

37
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:19,720
And everyone who has supported me along the way, including my chief of staff Natashia Scott and the entire office of the Lieutenant Governor.
感谢一路支持我的每一个人，包括办公厅主任娜塔莎·斯科特，以及副州长办公室全体同事。

38
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:25,300
I could not have done this without each and every one of you.
没有你们每一个人，我做不到这一切。

39
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:35,760
To my incredible friends, every person who volunteered, who endorsed me, who showed up any and every time you were called upon,
感谢我了不起的朋友，感谢每一个做志愿者、给予支持，以及每次受到召唤就出现的人，

40
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:39,700
You lifted me up and pushed me forward when I needed it the most.
在我最需要的时候，你们扶起我，推着我向前。

41
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:45,320
You believed in this campaign even on days when the path ahead wasn't clear.
即使前路不明，你们仍相信这场竞选。

42
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:54,220
To Senator Durbin and Senator Duckworth, thank you for your kind and inspirational words tonight.
感谢德宾参议员、达克沃思参议员，今晚给予温暖而鼓舞人心的讲话。

43
00:04:54,440 --> 00:05:03,910
I cannot wait to join our incredible soon-to-be senior senator Tammy Duckworth in Washington.
我迫不及待要去华盛顿，与即将成为本州资深参议员的塔米·达克沃思一起工作。

44
00:05:03,910 --> 00:05:14,430
And it's truly humbling that the people of Illinois have entrusted me to succeed a true public servant and personal hero of mine,
伊利诺伊人民托付我，在美国参议院接替一位真正的公仆、我个人心中的英雄，

45
00:05:14,990 --> 00:05:17,670
Senator Dick Durbin, in the United States Senate.
迪克·德宾参议员，这让我倍感谦卑。

46
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:39,080
And of course, to my family, my husband Brian, my rock, my person, my greatest source of strength,
当然，还要感谢家人，感谢丈夫布赖恩；我的磐石、我的伴侣、我最大的力量来源，

47
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:48,820
Who didn't just support me on this journey, but every day encouraged me, prayed over me, bolstered me up and shouldered the burden with me.
你不仅支持这段旅程，还每天鼓励我、为我祈祷、给我力量，与我一起承担重担。

48
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,480
I love you so much.
我非常爱你。

49
00:05:53,810 --> 00:06:07,930
To my brilliant and beautiful daughters, Tyler, Cassidy, Ryan, McKenzie, you are the reason why I fight.
感谢我聪明、美丽的女儿们：泰勒、卡西迪、赖恩、麦肯齐。你们是我奋斗的原因。

50
00:06:08,230 --> 00:06:16,990
You are my greatest joy and out of every title I could possibly hold, it is the greatest honor of my life to have the title mom.
你们是我最大的快乐；在我能拥有的所有头衔中，“妈妈”是我一生最珍惜的荣誉。

51
00:06:16,990 --> 00:06:20,030
I love you back.
我也爱你们。

52
00:06:20,030 --> 00:06:32,860
To my parents who are smiling down on us tonight and who have been looking over my shoulder every single day.
感谢我的父母，他们今晚正在天上微笑着看着我们，每一天都在守望我。

53
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,180
Thank you for paving the way.
谢谢你们，为我铺平道路。

54
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:45,300
I lost my mom Velma the day before I launched my first campaign for state representative after caring for her during her battle with Alzheimer's.
在我第一次宣布竞选州众议员的前一天，母亲维尔玛去世了；此前，我一直照顾着与阿尔茨海默病抗争的她。

55
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:50,920
And I lost my dad Henry last November in the middle of this campaign.
去年十一月，在这场竞选进行之中，父亲亨利也去世了。

56
00:06:52,040 --> 00:07:00,120
There were moments over the past 2 years when I wished more than anything that I could just pick up the phone and hear them on the other side.
过去两年，有些时刻，我无比渴望拿起电话，就能再次听见他们的声音。

57
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:07,640
But in a way I have because their voices, their stories, and everything that they poured into me,
但某种意义上，我确实听见了：他们的声音、故事，以及倾注给我的一切，

58
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:15,060
Their love, their faith, their commitment to service have been woven into the DNA of this campaign since the very start.
他们的爱、信仰、服务他人的承诺，从一开始就融入了这场竞选的血脉。

59
00:07:15,930 --> 00:07:22,800
My mother, a public school teacher, taught me to believe in the power of education and opportunity.
母亲是公立学校教师，她教会我相信教育和机会的力量。

60
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:32,800
My father, a Navy veteran who marched from Selma to Montgomery in 1965, taught me that when you see an injustice,
父亲是海军退伍军人，一九六五年曾参加从塞尔玛到蒙哥马利的游行。他教会我：看到不公，

61
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:36,600
You have a responsibility to do something about it.
就有责任采取行动。

62
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:47,820
And I know that they are so proud because tonight we sent a message loud and clear for them to hear all the way in Washington, D.C.
我知道，他们会无比自豪，因为今晚，我们发出的信息如此响亮，连华盛顿都能听见，连首都都能听见。

63
00:07:51,355 --> 00:07:55,610
That this seat belongs to the people of Illinois.
这个席位，属于伊利诺伊人民。

64
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:09,200
Listen, 2 months from now, when I walk into the United States capitol, I intend to remember exactly who sent me there,
两个月后，当我走进美国国会大厦，我会清楚记得，是谁把我送到那里，

65
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:10,940
Each and every one of you.
是你们每一个人。

66
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:19,320
I'll remember the people who looked me in the eye and trusted me to bring their voices to Washington.
我会记得那些直视我的眼睛、信任我能把他们的声音带到华盛顿的人。

67
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:26,300
I'll remember the people who shared their fears, their hopes, their struggles, and their dreams.
记得那些与我分享恐惧、希望、挣扎与梦想的人。

68
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:38,060
Over the course of this campaign, I met people who reminded me why this work matters, who reminded me what truly makes a democracy.
竞选中，我遇到许多人，让我想起这份工作为什么重要，什么才真正构成民主。

69
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:42,120
You see, democracy is not about Donald Trump.
民主，不是唐纳德·特朗普。

70
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:44,760
It's not about Congress.
不是国会。

71
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:51,760
It's not any one politician, one political party, or one seat in the Senate.
不是某个政客、某个政党，或参议院中的一个席位。

72
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:56,320
Democracy isn't something that we sit back and watch.
民主，不是我们坐着旁观的东西。

73
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:59,380
Democracy is something we do.
民主，是我们亲手实践的事情。

74
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:07,900
It's something we build brick by brick, conversation by conversation, neighbor by neighbor.
是我们一砖一瓦、一次次交谈、一个个邻里地建立起来的东西。

75
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:16,240
It's Angel who brought his grandparents to vote for the very first time after they became naturalized citizens.
是安赫尔，在祖父母入籍后，带他们第一次去投票。

76
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:27,940
It's Ms. Williams who served our country and now spends every day serving her community, making sure her neighbors have the resources they need to thrive.
是威廉姆斯女士，曾服务国家，如今每天服务社区，确保邻居获得生活发展所需的资源。

77
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:35,220
It's the mom with the whistle making sure every child in her neighborhood gets home from school safely.
是那个拿着哨子、确保街区每个孩子都能安全放学回家的母亲。

78
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:46,880
It's the student fellows who organized their campuses and made sure that young people had a seat at the table in this campaign.
是那些在校园组织同学、确保年轻人在这场竞选中拥有一席之地的学生。

79
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:57,823
It's the pastors I met in Carbondale, the healthcare providers in Peoria, the caregivers in Chicago, the small business owners in Edwardsville,
是我在卡本代尔遇见的牧师、皮奥里亚的医护人员、芝加哥的照护者、爱德华兹维尔的小企业主，

80
00:09:57,823 --> 00:10:01,067
The farmers in Abingdon.
阿宾登的农民。

81
00:10:01,067 --> 00:10:04,200
I'll never forget those moments or those people.
我永远不会忘记那些时刻、那些人。

82
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:11,460
The people who make up the rich fabric of this great state, who make me proud to be an Illinoisan,
他们织成这个伟大州丰富的生活图景，让我为身为伊利诺伊人而骄傲，

83
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:18,280
And who reminded me that democracy is alive wherever neighbors refuse to give up on each other.
也提醒我：只要邻里不放弃彼此，民主就活着。

84
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:25,160
They reminded me that democracy is also the joy we found along the way.
他们提醒我，民主也是我们沿途发现的快乐。

85
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:33,180
The recognition that we're in this together, the hope that we will wake up tomorrow feeling just a little bit lighter.
是明白我们同舟共济，是期待明天醒来，心头能稍微轻松一些。

86
00:10:33,180 --> 00:10:39,680
The reminder that from chaos can come community and coalition and change.
是记住：混乱之中，也能生出社区、联盟和改变。

87
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:54,940
And yes, for me joy is also lacing up a pair of roller skates or making it clear that your next United States Senator is in fact a house head who loves To dance.
对我来说，快乐也可以是系好轮滑鞋，或让大家知道，你们下一任美国参议员，其实是一位热爱跳舞的浩室音乐迷。

88
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:03,340
Listen, there's a lot to be scared about.
眼下，确实有很多令人害怕的事。

89
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:08,740
There's a lot to be angry about, but joy is resistance.
有很多令人愤怒的事，但快乐本身就是抵抗。

90
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:15,220
And I believe in my soul that the joy that I have the world didn't give it.
我发自灵魂深处地相信：我的快乐，不是这个世界赐予的。

91
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:17,460
So, the world can't take it away.
所以，这个世界也夺不走。

92
00:11:20,230 --> 00:11:24,950
We can never let anyone steal our joy from us.
我们永远不能让任何人偷走自己的快乐。

93
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:34,050
Because if we want to be ready for the fight ahead we're going to need that joy and we're going to need the strength that we find in one another.
要准备好面对前方的斗争，我们需要这份快乐，也需要从彼此身上汲取的力量。

94
00:11:34,950 --> 00:11:42,770
For 2 years we've been hard at work organizing and showing up nonstop.
两年来，我们努力组织、不断行动，从不停歇。

95
00:11:43,590 --> 00:11:47,170
But this campaign was never about election day.
但这场竞选从来不只关乎选举日。

96
00:11:47,610 --> 00:11:52,410
It's about every day that comes after because now we get to work.
它关乎此后的每一天，因为现在，我们要开始工作了。

97
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:59,890
Since day one of this campaign you've told me that the status quo isn't working.
从竞选第一天起，你们就告诉我，现状行不通。

98
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:08,810
Some months you're wondering whether you can afford groceries, rent, and child care without having to choose which bill goes unpaid.
有些月份，你们不知道能否同时支付食品、房租和托育，而不必拖欠某一张账单。

99
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:17,730
Despite working full-time and doing everything right, you're still wondering if you can actually get ahead.
即使全职工作、做对所有该做的事，你们仍在怀疑，自己到底能否过上更好的生活。

100
00:12:18,490 --> 00:12:25,230
You're watching the chaos and the dysfunction coming out of Washington and asking whose side are they on?
你们看着华盛顿的混乱与失能，问：他们究竟站在哪一边？

101
00:12:26,430 --> 00:12:28,830
None of it is by accident.
这一切，都不是偶然。

102
00:12:29,810 --> 00:12:36,750
The corruption in Washington is directly connected to the struggles people face around their kitchen tables.
华盛顿的腐败，与人们家中餐桌旁面对的生活困境，直接相连。

103
00:12:37,630 --> 00:12:47,250
Working families have been left to pick up the tab for the wealthy and well-connected, while the crook in the oval office enriches himself and his allies.
劳动家庭被迫替富人和权贵买单，而椭圆形办公室里的骗子，却让自己和盟友不断致富。

104
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:55,550
And then those same corrupt politicians have the nerve to tell people to be patient.
随后，那些腐败政客居然还有脸叫人民耐心等候。

105
00:12:56,770 --> 00:13:00,510
Well, I'm here to tell you that we are done waiting.
而我要告诉你们：我们不再等了。

106
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:08,920
When I became a state representative in 2017, people told me, "Don't ruffle too many feathers.
二〇一七年，我成为州众议员时，人们对我说：“别得罪太多人。

107
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:11,400
Don't make too many waves.
别掀起太大风浪。

108
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:12,680
You're a freshman.
你还是新人。

109
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:13,760
Sit back.
先坐在后面。

110
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:14,920
Just learn."
好好学着。”

111
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:21,229
Well, I ignored that advice then.
当时，我没有听从这些建议。

112
00:13:21,310 --> 00:13:26,670
And I certainly won't be sitting back and listening quietly when I get to Washington, D.C.
到了华盛顿，我当然更不会坐在后面，安静地听着。

113
00:13:26,670 --> 00:13:45,140
I'm going to fight loudly for affordable health care, for reproductive freedom, for workers' rights, for voting rights,
我会大声争取负担得起的医疗、生育自主权、劳动者权利和投票权，

114
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:51,200
And for the families who are doing everything right and still struggling to get ahead.
也会为那些做对一切、却仍在艰难谋生的家庭而战。

115
00:13:52,060 --> 00:14:04,900
I'm going to fight boldly for our farmers, our caregivers, our small businesses, our public schools, our immigrant communities,
我会勇敢地为农民、照护者、小企业、公立学校、移民社区，

116
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:14,860
And the next generation of Illinoisans who deserve the opportunity to build a good life right here at home.
以及下一代伊利诺伊人而战；他们值得在家乡拥有建立美好生活的机会。

117
00:14:15,790 --> 00:14:25,240
And I'm going to fight compassionately for each and every one of you, including including those who didn't vote for me.
我会心怀同理，为你们每一个人奋斗，也包括没有投票给我的人。

118
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,980
Never forget this.
永远不要忘记。

119
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:32,720
There is more that unites us than divides us.
让我们团结的东西，远多于使我们分裂的东西。

120
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:41,200
We are united in our struggles, and we can be united in our solutions, too.
我们有共同的困境，也能一起找到共同的解决办法。

121
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:55,720
And when I'm voting in the Senate, it will be on behalf of all 12.8 million Illinoisans who I have been given the privilege of representing.
在参议院投票时，我将代表我有幸服务的全部一千二百八十万伊利诺伊人。

122
00:14:56,780 --> 00:15:02,980
Now, I can't promise that we're going to agree on everything, but I can promise that I will never stop listening,
我无法保证我们在每件事上都意见一致，但我保证，我永远不会停止倾听，

123
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:06,920
Never stop showing up, and never stop fighting for you.
不会停止出现，更不会停止为你们奋斗。

124
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:13,800
And I will never confuse being elected with being entitled to this job.
我绝不会把“当选”，误当成自己理所当然拥有这份工作。

125
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:21,940
I'm headed to Washington to do the people's business.
我去华盛顿，是为了处理人民的事务。

126
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:24,020
Your business.
你们的事务。

127
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:29,100
So, I ask you to hold me accountable.
所以，请你们监督我，要求我负责。

128
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:32,240
You knocked on doors to get me here.
你们敲门，把我送到这里。

129
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,520
You can knock on my door to make sure I'm doing the job.
你们也可以敲我的门，确保我在好好工作。

130
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:39,500
You made calls for my campaign.
你们为我的竞选打过电话。

131
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:41,440
You can call my office.
你们也可以给我的办公室打电话。

132
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:46,080
You can tell me when we're getting it right and when we're getting it wrong.
告诉我，哪些事做对了，哪些事做错了。

133
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,000
You can challenge me.
你们可以质疑我。

134
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:53,620
You can push me because, like I said, this seat belongs to you.
可以督促我，因为正如我所说，这个席位属于你们。

135
00:15:55,280 --> 00:16:04,619
Senator Durbin reminded me last week that it was this very seat that Abraham Lincoln and Stephen Douglas debated for.
德宾参议员上周提醒我，亚伯拉罕·林肯和斯蒂芬·道格拉斯，当年争夺的正是这个席位。

136
00:16:05,090 --> 00:16:09,800
And those debates boiled down to one issue, slavery.
那些辩论归结起来，关乎一个问题：奴隶制。

137
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:20,940
That debate set into motion a chain of events that would lead Lincoln to become president and one day issue the Emancipation Proclamation,
那场辩论引发了一连串事件，最终让林肯成为总统，并有一天颁布《解放奴隶宣言》，

138
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:29,460
Freeing my great-great-grandfather, William Stevens, allowing him and his brother to build a town in Mississippi.
解放了我的高祖父威廉·史蒂文斯，让他和兄弟得以在密西西比州建立一个小镇。

139
00:16:30,140 --> 00:16:36,940
And enabling his great-great-granddaughter to become the first black lieutenant governor of Illinois.
也让他的玄孙女，得以成为伊利诺伊州第一位黑人副州长。

140
00:16:43,642 --> 00:16:55,140
And now now the seat where the future of slavery was once debated will be held by a descendant of someone who was enslaved.
而如今，这个曾经辩论奴隶制未来的席位，将由一位被奴役者的后代担任。

141
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:09,040
That progress was possible because people not only believed that things could change but demanded that they did.
这样的进步之所以可能，是因为人们不仅相信事情能改变，更要求改变真正发生。

142
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:23,020
It was possible because of the courage of people who refused to accept the limits placed on them because of the relentless work to ensure that the next generation would go further
因为人们勇敢地拒绝接受强加在自己身上的限制，坚持不懈地努力，确保下一代能够走得更远，

143
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:23,920
Than the last.
超越上一代。

144
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:32,880
I don't take the history of this seat lightly because I know that I did not get here alone.
我不会轻视这个席位的历史，因为我知道，自己绝非独自走到这里。

145
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:41,100
I stand on the shoulders of William Stevens who built a town and a future.
我站在威廉·史蒂文斯的肩膀上；他建设了一个小镇，也建设了一个未来。

146
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:48,800
I stand on the shoulders of Velma, who taught, and Henry, who marched.
站在教书的维尔玛、参加游行的亨利的肩膀上。

147
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:57,432
I stand on the shoulders of Carol Moseley Braun.
站在卡罗尔·莫斯利·布劳恩的肩膀上。

148
00:17:57,530 --> 00:17:59,830
Who overcame all the odds.
她克服了重重艰难。

149
00:18:00,550 --> 00:18:08,150
I stand on the shoulders of everyone who came before me, who fought for opportunities they would never live to see.
站在所有先行者的肩膀上；他们为那些自己一生都无法亲见的机会而奋斗。

150
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:12,030
And look how far we've come together.
看看我们一起，已经走了多远。

151
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:15,890
That is the promise of America.
这就是美国的承诺。

152
00:18:16,650 --> 00:18:24,170
That is the promise of democracy and that is the promise we have to keep honoring every single day.
这就是民主的承诺，是我们必须每一天继续兑现的承诺。

153
00:18:25,170 --> 00:18:29,910
Illinois our story is far from finished.
伊利诺伊，我们的故事还远没有结束。

154
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:33,850
And our chapters are still ahead.
新的篇章，还在前方。

155
00:18:34,830 --> 00:18:36,250
We have each other.
我们拥有彼此。

156
00:18:36,930 --> 00:18:38,970
We have our voices.
我们拥有自己的声音。

157
00:18:39,870 --> 00:18:41,370
We have our joy.
我们拥有自己的快乐。

158
00:18:41,790 --> 00:18:47,550
And we have a sacred responsibility to make tomorrow better than today.
我们也肩负神圣的责任，让明天比今天更好。

159
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:50,150
So, let's get to work.
所以，让我们开始工作。

160
00:18:50,550 --> 00:18:51,790
Thank you.
谢谢。

161
00:18:51,970 --> 00:18:53,070
God bless you.
愿上帝保佑你们。

162
00:18:53,450 --> 00:18:55,170
And God bless Illinois.
愿上帝保佑伊利诺伊州。